            "text": "{\"description\":\"The first photograph shows a tall carved stone with a broad lower body and a narrower upper head/neck area. On the visible front are shallow incised and raised lines, including paired eye-like hollows, curving bands across the lower front, a central raised circular disk, and several worn linear figures near the upper section. The surface is rough and eroded, making some details hard to read.\",\"avian\":{\"answer\":\"uncertain\",\"evidence\":\"There are worn linear carvings on the upper front, but no clearly readable bird body or birdlike head/beak is visible in the first photograph.\",\"box\":null},\"large_face\":{\"answer\":\"uncertain\",\"evidence\":\"The front has two eye-like hollows and curved lines that could suggest a face-like arrangement, but distinct human facial features are not clearly carved enough to identify a large human face.\",\"box\":null},\"scorpion\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"No carved figure with multiple legs and a segmented upturned tail is visible on the main stone surface.\",\"box\":null},\"round_motif\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"A distinct raised circular disk is carved near the middle of the front, separate from the eye-like hollows and lower repair-like mark.\",\"box\":[0.401,0.535,0.554,0.619]},\"three_arches\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"Although there are multiple curved bands near the lower front, they are nested arcs rather than three arch-topped forms side by side in a row.\",\"box\":null},\"limitations\":\"Warm lighting, erosion, rough stone texture, and shallow worn incisions make the upper carvings and possible figures difficult to interpret.\"}",
